<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sabarkantha district</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sabarkantha is a district of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, named after the Sabarmati river, with its headquarters at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himmatnagar">Himmatnagar</a>. It was formed in 1949 from Idar and many small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahi-kantha-agency">Mahi Kantha Agency</a>, which had been merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Bombay</a> Province, and became part of Gujarat when that state was created in 1960.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sabarkantha-district.jpg" alt="Sabarkantha district" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Snehrashmi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roda_Temples-17.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Idar acceded to India and in 1948 was merged into Bombay State; since 1960 its lands, centred on Himmatnagar, are in <b>Sabarkantha district</b> of Gujarat.</blockquote><a href="/state/idar-state">Idar State</a></li><li><blockquote>Ilol was merged into Bombay Province in 1948 and became part of Gujarat in 1960, in present <b>Sabarkantha district</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/ilol-state">Ilol State</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1948 Mohanpur was merged into Bombay Province, and its villages became part of <b>Sabarkantha district</b> in Gujarat in 1960.</blockquote><a href="/state/mohanpur-state">Mohanpur State</a></li><li><blockquote>Pal merged into Bombay Province in 1948 and became part of Gujarat in 1960, in <b>Sabarkantha district</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/pal-state">Pal State</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1948 the state was merged into Bombay Province, and its territory became part of <b>Sabarkantha district</b> when Gujarat was formed in 1960.</blockquote><a href="/state/vijaynagar-state">Vijaynagar State</a></li></ul></section>
